# Dev Server & Visual QA

## Do not start the dev server

- Never run `npm start`, `npm run dev`, `npx serve`, or equivalent commands to start a local server.
- The user starts and stops the dev server manually.
- If a server is needed to verify something, ask the user to start it first — do not start it yourself.

## Look and feel is owned by the user

- The user handles all visual review: layout, spacing, typography, colors, responsive behavior, dark mode, and overall polish.
- Do not use browser automation, screenshots, or MCP browser tools to check appearance unless the user explicitly asks.
- After UI changes, summarize what changed in code/CSS and let the user verify in the browser.
- Do not ask the user to confirm visual details you could only judge by running the site yourself.

## What you should still do

- Implement requested UI/CSS/HTML/JS changes correctly.
- Run non-visual checks when appropriate (e.g. unit tests, lint) if the user asks or the task requires it.
- Flag likely visual risks in prose (e.g. "Grön SVG may invert oddly in dark mode") without attempting to preview them.
